{"id":"a68d4678-4f0a-40e7-817d-544bf2abb8dd","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"56167a99d54a3c84","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/debug-protocol.ts","baseline":{"blob":"cd36ced3ad28a26e4c42cbb36a3fb737b79e093c","start":2524,"end":2698},"shape":{"type":"TypeLiteral","atoms":["{","\"","type","\"",":","\"","explore","\"",";","\"","source","\"",":","string",";","\"","fileName","\"",":","string",";","\"","policy","\"","?",":","Policy",";","\"","args","\"","?",":","string","[]",";","\"","eventLoop","\"",":","LoopStart",";","\"","maxRuns","\"","?",":","number",";","\"","workspace","\"","?",":","SharedArrayBuffer","}"]},"context":{"before":"0bdf6645cb2a6f75","after":"41d14434de5a0daf"}},"payload":{"text":"Run every ordering of the program's events (tsval's explore) instead of debugging it: answered with `explored`.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:08:51.216Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:08:51.216Z"}
{"id":"af5bbe4c-efdc-4e2b-ab3d-1b9795eb3237","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"89e56fb91a262a33","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/debug-protocol.ts","baseline":{"blob":"79a60c57fe6e0ef5f56df8bcc387657799bfd639","start":1746,"end":1865},"shape":{"type":"ExportDeclaration","atoms":["export","interface","Crash","{","\"","line","\"",":","number",";","\"","at","\"",":","[","number",",","number","]",";","\"","message","\"",":","string",";","\"","file","\"","?",":","string",";","\"","stopped","\"","?",":","true","}"]},"context":{"before":"37d7d0dacddf682a","after":"24ec69651abdf021"}},"payload":{"text":"Where a program threw: its line and range — in `file`, when that's another of its files than the entry.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:08:55.643Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:08:55.643Z"}
{"id":"b8405838-dca2-48a1-932a-8fffff4bc5e5","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"f244a0f8afc5841f","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/debug-protocol.ts","baseline":{"blob":"d90d322e24bcfb5e920ef03c16c3ed34cfe230cf","start":8542,"end":8582},"shape":{"type":"TypeLiteral","atoms":["{","\"","type","\"",":","\"","serving","\"",";","\"","ports","\"",":","number","[]","}"]},"context":{"before":"aa66f82f5b9b2908","after":"dd79d8af11d40a99"}},"payload":{"text":"Out of work, serving: the session is idle until a request (or a timer) comes.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:08:11.291Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:08:11.291Z"}
{"id":"b8f897ca-a6a1-4cb8-bd06-0cbecb76d49a","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"1b1cfcb691e13e68","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/debug-protocol.ts","baseline":{"blob":"f041c96bc1d82bfccd982cd31d0401b4097ee0e9","start":4371,"end":4543},"shape":{"type":"ExportDeclaration","atoms":["export","interface","Ordering","{","\"","output","\"",":","Printed","[]",";","\"","crash","\"","?",":","{","\"","message","\"",":","string",";","\"","file","\"","?",":","string",";","\"","line","\"","?",":","number","}",";","\"","schedule","\"",":","number","[]",";","\"","path","\"",":","string","[]",";","\"","runs","\"",":","number","}"]},"context":{"before":"e6522924607defdd","after":"006502713ecb03d0"}},"payload":{"text":"One way a run of the program can end, from exploring its orderings: what it printed and where, where it threw if it did,\na schedule that gets there (to debug it), the events chosen along it, and how many runs ended this way.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:08:38.295Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:08:38.295Z"}
{"id":"c301470c-5ed1-44d0-8e54-8be86686a32a","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"18da4738468dfd78","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/debug-protocol.ts","baseline":{"blob":"cae1e8fa71cbbb80647d8c071f34b334a6a1074e","start":3613,"end":3656},"shape":{"type":"TypeLiteral","atoms":["{","\"","type","\"",":","\"","pace","\"",";","\"","pace","\"",":","\"","real","\"","|","\"","fast","\"","}"]},"context":{"before":"57815b7ca66f33e5","after":"ff9459778e4a17ee"}},"payload":{"text":"What a timer's wait costs from here on: its real delay, or none (Skip Waits).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:08:45.545Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:08:45.545Z"}
{"id":"c3e6cd4a-5707-42bf-b1db-cfc216fdaeda","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"727b4a32ab57fa6b","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/debug-protocol.ts","baseline":{"blob":"0f19977b89a728939ea9b4222168d57dadae73f5","start":0,"end":105},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","type","{","CoverageEvent",",","Effect",",","LiveBatch",",","TestReport",",","RulePlace","}","from","\"","@brianjenkins94/editor-api","\""]},"context":{"after":"6a894ad1c5672e01"}},"payload":{"text":"The tsval debugger's adapter ⇄ worker protocol, over the pod hub. Each session has two subjects: control goes DOWN\n(`debug.session.<id>.control`, adapter → worker) and events come UP (`debug.session.<id>.event`, worker → adapter),\nso several sessions share the pod hub without crossing. A control message that starts work carries the adapter\naction's trace context in the hub envelope, so the worker's step continues that trace.\n\nThe one thing that isn't a message: resuming from a breakpoint inside a host-invoked guest call (a server's handler,\na library's callback).\nThe worker is blocked in Atomics.wait there, so the adapter resumes it through the shared control word it sent at\nlaunch.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:08:59.987Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:08:59.987Z"}
{"id":"c55abb1c-f1d7-497d-a01f-b0a3875f3643","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"ee2ca221f9e3927b","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/debug-protocol.ts","baseline":{"blob":"2ac02ebf17318ce866553ae84fbb24abb4b3935c","start":7757,"end":7833},"shape":{"type":"TypeLiteral","atoms":["{","\"","type","\"",":","\"","values","\"",";","\"","batch","\"",":","LiveBatch",";","\"","file","\"","?",":","string",";","\"","source","\"","?",":","string","}"]},"context":{"before":"0334e069219835d3","after":"8f273faa5ddeba27"}},"payload":{"text":"Live values new since the last, of the entry or (`file`) another of the program's files, with its text (`source`) the\nfirst time: a few times a second, and before a stop or the end.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:08:17.450Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:08:17.450Z"}
{"id":"ce7aec4e-24a5-4fe9-a03d-764af38e6b09","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"cfbc66468501bfec","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/debug-protocol.ts","baseline":{"blob":"7718ee2baca7a37c28b4951fb52dd776d167ad2d","start":7210,"end":7312},"shape":{"type":"TypeLiteral","atoms":["{","\"","type","\"",":","\"","recorded","\"",";","\"","capability","\"",":","string",";","\"","resource","\"",":","string",";","\"","value","\"",":","unknown",";","\"","request","\"","?",":","string","}"]},"context":{"before":"dc4efabc16be5cc5","after":"9edc3ddd46210e1d"}},"payload":{"text":"What an allowed call returned, for what's given back when it isn't made.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:08:20.596Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:08:20.596Z"}
{"id":"ddb2be5b-67a3-4f49-8093-7a90378eb53e","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"e0cdd3fea9bb564d","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/debug-protocol.ts","baseline":{"blob":"abf6cadfa11800e50bad8b61003bd282dd44b951","start":6030,"end":6243},"shape":{"type":"ExportDeclaration","atoms":["export","interface","CapabilityAsk","{","\"","line","\"",":","number",";","\"","at","\"","?",":","[","number",",","number","]",";","\"","capability","\"",":","string",";","\"","callee","\"",":","string",";","\"","resource","\"",":","string",";","\"","resolved","\"",":","boolean",";","\"","dangerous","\"",":","boolean",";","\"","file","\"","?",":","string",";","\"","source","\"","?",":","string","}"]},"context":{"before":"8b65190bd594efdb","after":"b1963c992f02c4de"}},"payload":{"text":"What a capability stop asks (RUNTIME-EVIDENCE.md, *Capability decisions, on the line*): the gated call on the line it stopped at — its capability,\nits callee as written, and the resource it would reach, from the run's own values where they're known by then (a\nliteral, a variable's value), else the argument as written. `line` is 0-based.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:08:29.373Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:08:29.373Z"}
{"id":"e526a328-8481-4ff3-b355-27c1deb14785","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"f124d8845f740264","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/debug-protocol.ts","baseline":{"blob":"1215dff60dd7133ab6d685d69ff3536bee929d42","start":8193,"end":8289},"shape":{"type":"TypeLiteral","atoms":["{","\"","type","\"",":","\"","valueSet","\"",";","\"","ok","\"",":","boolean",";","\"","value","\"","?",":","string",";","\"","error","\"","?",":","string",";","\"","snapshot","\"","?",":","Snapshot","}"]},"context":{"before":"781e0fa304a0edf8","after":"70cad7b3afaf45f5"}},"payload":{"text":"A `setValue` done (the new value as the Variables view shows it, and the stop's snapshot with it), or refused.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:08:14.237Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:08:14.237Z"}
{"id":"e5ac1d5f-fd54-48e9-ab05-05149209ee2a","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"19c8734dfc5f516d","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/debug-protocol.ts","baseline":{"blob":"3289c63bfb689cd6586c79a09d456bca6aa147ff","start":8672,"end":8690},"shape":{"type":"TypeLiteral","atoms":["{","\"","type","\"",":","\"","busy","\"","}"]},"context":{"before":"f244a0f8afc5841f","after":"fd1110a3e2328387"}},"payload":{"text":"The program is computing, every few seconds while it runs code (the run contract's `busy`).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:08:09.753Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:08:09.753Z"}
{"id":"e6fd0b56-280d-4b5e-aba1-cbd847f6f487","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"dc4efabc16be5cc5","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/extensions/tsval/debug-protocol.ts","baseline":{"blob":"96848dd59c5ec4ccc5fd21cb66d70af7eb86f198","start":6860,"end":6938},"shape":{"type":"TypeLiteral","atoms":["{","\"","type","\"",":","\"","terminated","\"",";","\"","exitCode","\"","?",":","number",";","\"","crash","\"","?",":","Crash",";","\"","quiet","\"","?",":","true","}"]},"context":{"before":"398c2280a2270fda","after":"0f2b2eb9f19c367e"}},"payload":{"text":"The program is over: `exitCode` 1 when it threw, else 0.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:08:24.898Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:08:24.898Z"}
